WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.024
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level four.

2
00:00:06.324 --> 00:00:10.232
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.532 --> 00:00:17.852
Unit seven: Nuclear Non-Proliferation. Today you will urge overdue action with It is high time + past simple.

4
00:00:18.152 --> 00:00:20.781
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:24.978
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.817 --> 00:00:27.038
Nuclear weapon.

7
00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:32.337
Nuclear weapon means a bomb that releases huge destructive power from atoms.

8
00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.600
A single nuclear weapon could destroy a city.

9
00:00:36.183 --> 00:00:39.068
Your turn. Say: Nuclear weapon.

10
00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:43.329
Nuclear weapon.

11
00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:45.665
Non-proliferation treaty.

12
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:52.074
Non-proliferation treaty means an agreement to stop nuclear weapons spreading to more countries.

13
00:00:52.683 --> 00:00:55.995
The non-proliferation treaty has nearly universal support.

14
00:00:56.583 --> 00:01:00.234
Your turn. Say: Non-proliferation treaty.

15
00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.076
Non-proliferation treaty.

16
00:01:05.817 --> 00:01:07.038
Arms control.

17
00:01:08.050 --> 00:01:12.012
Arms control means agreements that limit the number or type of weapons.

18
00:01:12.617 --> 00:01:14.941
Arms control talks resumed in spring.

19
00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:18.620
Your turn. Say: Arms control.

20
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:22.944
Arms control.

21
00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:25.207
Nuclear deterrence.

22
00:01:26.217 --> 00:01:30.945
Nuclear deterrence means the idea that fear of a nuclear reply prevents an attack.

23
00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.757
Nuclear deterrence has divided strategists for decades.

24
00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:38.560
Your turn. Say: Nuclear deterrence.

25
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.970
Nuclear deterrence.

26
00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:44.753
Disarmament.

27
00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:49.212
Disarmament means the process of reducing or removing weapons.

28
00:01:49.817 --> 00:01:52.246
Disarmament began with the oldest missiles.

29
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.653
Your turn. Say: Disarmament.

30
00:01:58.500 --> 00:01:59.594
Disarmament.

31
00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.827
Uranium enrichment.

32
00:02:02.817 --> 00:02:07.870
Uranium enrichment means the process that makes uranium strong enough for reactors or bombs.

33
00:02:08.483 --> 00:02:10.970
Uranium enrichment is closely monitored.

34
00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:14.259
Your turn. Say: Uranium enrichment.

35
00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:18.682
Uranium enrichment.

36
00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:21.161
International inspection.

37
00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:28.550
International inspection means checks carried out by outside experts to confirm a country keeps its promises.

38
00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:32.473
International inspection confirmed the closure of the plant.

39
00:02:33.083 --> 00:02:36.223
Your turn. Say: International inspection.

40
00:02:39.067 --> 00:02:40.776
International inspection.

41
00:02:41.517 --> 00:02:42.843
Nuclear power.

42
00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:47.754
Nuclear power means electricity produced using the energy of atoms.

43
00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:51.511
Nuclear power supplies a third of the country's electricity.

44
00:02:52.117 --> 00:02:55.280
Your turn. Say: Nuclear power.

45
00:02:58.133 --> 00:02:59.622
Nuclear power.

46
00:03:00.433 --> 00:03:03.980
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:10.929
Visal, a diplomat says 'It is high time states agreed to disarm.' Why is 'agreed' in the past tense?

48
00:03:12.017 --> 00:03:21.867
After 'It is (about/high) time', we use the past simple for a present or future need. It is an unreal past: the action should already be happening.

49
00:03:22.983 --> 00:03:24.820
Are there similar structures?

50
00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:37.404
Yes: 'I would rather inspectors visited the site' and 'Suppose a state refused'. All use the past simple to talk about a present or future preference or possibility.

51
00:03:38.517 --> 00:03:39.912
Can I use 'would' after it?

52
00:03:41.017 --> 00:03:51.241
Not in this pattern. We say 'It's time they ended the programme', not 'they would end'. The simple form 'It's time to end it' is also correct.

53
00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.993
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:59.381
Grammar focus: Unreal past: It is high time plus past simple.

55
00:03:59.681 --> 00:04:00.798
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:01.483 --> 00:04:05.131
It is high time states agreed to a full disarmament plan.

57
00:04:06.017 --> 00:04:08.991
I would rather inspectors visited every enrichment site.

58
00:04:09.883 --> 00:04:13.218
It's about time the superpowers reduced their nuclear weapons.

59
00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:22.961
Use It is (high) time + subject + past simple for something that should already be happening. Also: would rather + subject + past simple.

60
00:04:23.717 --> 00:04:27.669
Be careful! Don't say: It is time we will act now.

61
00:04:29.633 --> 00:04:31.691
Say: It is time we acted now.

62
00:04:31.991 --> 00:04:34.397
Use the past simple after 'It is time'.

63
00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.852
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:40.794
Controlling the Most Dangerous Weapons.

65
00:04:41.094 --> 00:04:46.542
A single nuclear weapon can destroy a city, so non-proliferation is a global priority.

66
00:04:47.533 --> 00:04:53.759
The non-proliferation treaty asks states to avoid building weapons while keeping nuclear power for peaceful use.

67
00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:59.135
Many experts say it is high time the great powers moved towards real disarmament.

68
00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:05.744
Because uranium enrichment can serve peace or war, international inspection is essential.

69
00:05:06.733 --> 00:05:11.589
Arms control builds trust, and trust makes nuclear deterrence less dangerous.

70
00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:16.713
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.026
It is high time the government blank action.

72
00:05:20.326 --> 00:05:23.874
A, takes. B, took. C, will take.

73
00:05:27.433 --> 00:05:29.085
The answer is B: took.

74
00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:33.248
The process of reducing or removing weapons is blank.

75
00:05:33.548 --> 00:05:37.654
A, disarmament. B, enrichment. C, inspection.

76
00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.292
The answer is A: disarmament.

77
00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:46.159
Choose the correct sentence.

78
00:05:46.459 --> 00:05:53.364
A, It's time they end the programme.. B, It's time they ended the programme.. C, It's time they will end the programme..

79
00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:00.037
The answer is B: It's time they ended the programme..

80
00:06:01.183 --> 00:06:04.855
Checks carried out by outside experts are international blank.

81
00:06:05.155 --> 00:06:09.377
A, inspections. B, campaigns. C, elections.

82
00:06:12.933 --> 00:06:14.956
The answer is A: inspections.

83
00:06:16.117 --> 00:06:19.684
According to the reading, what can a single nuclear weapon do?

84
00:06:19.984 --> 00:06:24.763
A, destroy a city. B, fund a treaty. C, enrich uranium.

85
00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.706
The answer is A: destroy a city.

86
00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:35.098
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:39.958
Why do countries agree to international inspections of their nuclear programs?

88
00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.343
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:50.643 --> 00:07:17.888
Countries accept international inspections because they build trust. When independent experts confirm that uranium enrichment serves only peaceful nuclear power, neighbours feel safer and fewer states are tempted to build their own weapons. Inspections can also help to end sanctions and show that a government keeps its promises under the non-proliferation treaty.

90
00:07:18.188 --> 00:07:19.897
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:20.783 --> 00:07:27.035
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and unreal past: it is high time plus past simple.

92
00:07:27.335 --> 00:07:32.913
Today's value is global responsibility. Act as someone who belongs to the whole world.

93
00:07:33.213 --> 00:07:35.726
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

94
00:07:36.026 --> 00:07:38.934
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

